---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Nawtch"
  description="Nawtch's privacy policy. No account is required and your food, weight, and workout data stays on your device — here's exactly what limited analytics and advertising data is collected."
  canonicalPath="/privacy/"
  bodyClass="privacy"
>
  <header>
    <div class="header-left">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">Effective date: August 6, 2026</p>
    </div>
    <a class="ghost-btn" href="#" onclick="window.history.back(); return false;">← Back</a>
  </header>

  <div class="settings-section">
    <div class="settings-section-body">
      <p class="settings-desc">
        Nawtch ("Nawtch," "we," "us") operates the free web application available at <a href="https://nawtch.app" target="_blank" rel="noopener">https://nawtch.app</a> (the "Service"). This
        Privacy Policy explains what information is and isn't collected when you use the Service, and how it's
        handled.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="settings-section">
    <h2 class="settings-section-title">The Short Version</h2>
    <div class="settings-section-body">
      <p class="settings-desc">
        Nawtch does not require an account, and your food logs, weight history, custom foods, workout programs,
        and settings are stored entirely on your own device using your browser's local storage (IndexedDB).
        This information is never transmitted to Nawtch, and we have no server-side database of your personal
        tracking data — because we don't have a server at all. If you clear your browser's site data, this
        information is permanently lost, and Nawtch cannot recover it.
        <br /><br />
        The only data collected about your use of the Service is limited, aggregate usage analytics and
        advertising-related data, described below.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="settings-section">
    <h2 class="settings-section-title">Information We Do NOT Collect</h2>
    <div class="settings-section-body">
      <p class="settings-desc">We do not collect, receive, or store:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Your food, calorie, macro, or cost logs</li>
        <li>Your weight history</li>
        <li>Your workout programs or exercise data</li>
        <li>Any personal profile information, since no account exists</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="settings-desc" style="margin-top:10px;">
        All of the above stays on your device, in your browser, under your control.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="settings-section">
    <h2 class="settings-section-title">Information Collected via Third-Party Services</h2>
    <div class="settings-section-body">
      <p class="settings-desc">
        <strong>Google Analytics (GA4).</strong> We use Google Analytics to understand general usage of the
        Service — for example, which pages are visited and how often. This includes standard analytics data
        such as approximate location (derived from IP address), device and browser type, and general
        engagement metrics. This data is not linked to any Nawtch account, because none exists. You can learn
        more about how Google Analytics handles data at <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener">policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites</a>.
        <br /><br />
        <strong>Google AdSense.</strong> Nawtch is supported by advertising served through Google AdSense.
        AdSense may use cookies or similar technologies to serve ads and measure their performance.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          For users in the European Economic Area, the UK, and Switzerland, we currently serve only <strong>non-personalized ads</strong>, meaning ads are not based on your individual browsing history
          or interests. This may change in the future; if it does, we will update this policy and obtain any
          consent required by law through a certified consent management platform before doing so.
        </li>
        <li>
          For users elsewhere, ads served through AdSense may be personalized based on data Google collects
          across sites, in accordance with Google's own policies. You can review and adjust your ad
          personalization settings at <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">adssettings.google.com</a>, and learn more about interest-based advertising opt-outs at <a href="https://optout.aboutads.info" target="_blank" rel="noopener">optout.aboutads.info</a> (US) or <a href="https://www.youronlinechoices.eu" target="_blank" rel="noopener">youronlinechoices.eu</a> (EU).
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="settings-desc" style="margin-top:10px;">
        <strong>Open Food Facts.</strong> Barcode scanning works by sending the scanned barcode directly from
        your browser to the Open Food Facts API to retrieve product information. This request is made directly
        by your browser to Open Food Facts — Nawtch does not see, store, or process this data on any server of
        ours. Open Food Facts' handling of this request is governed by their own privacy policy, available on
        their website.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="settings-section">
    <h2 class="settings-section-title">Cookies and Local Storage</h2>
    <div class="settings-section-body">
      <p class="settings-desc">The Service uses:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Browser local storage (IndexedDB)</strong> to store your tracking data and settings, entirely on your device.</li>
        <li><strong>Cookies from Google Analytics and Google AdSense</strong>, as described above, for analytics and advertising purposes.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="settings-desc" style="margin-top:10px;">
        We do not use cookies or tracking of any kind to identify you personally or to build a profile of you
        across other websites ourselves — any such cross-site profiling that occurs is performed by Google as
        described in their own policies, not by Nawtch.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="settings-section">
    <h2 class="settings-section-title">Your Rights</h2>
    <div class="settings-section-body">
      <p class="settings-desc">
        Depending on where you live, you may have rights under laws such as the GDPR (EEA/UK) or the CCPA
        (California) regarding personal data, including rights to access, delete, or object to processing of
        your data. Because Nawtch does not maintain accounts or store personal tracking data on any server,
        there is generally no personal data held by us to access or delete beyond the limited analytics and
        advertising data described above, which is processed by Google on our behalf. You can exercise rights
        related to that data directly through the Google tools linked above, or contact us at the address below
        with any questions.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="settings-section">
    <h2 class="settings-section-title">Children's Privacy</h2>
    <div class="settings-section-body">
      <p class="settings-desc">
        The Service is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information
        from children.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="settings-section">
    <h2 class="settings-section-title">Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <div class="settings-section-body">
      <p class="settings-desc">
        We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Changes will be posted on this page with an
        updated effective date.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="settings-section">
    <h2 class="settings-section-title">Contact</h2>
    <div class="settings-section-body">
      <p class="settings-desc">
        Questions about this policy can be sent to <a href="mailto:team@nawtch.app">team@nawtch.app</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
